---
description: Investigate and draft a publication-ready security advisory
argument-hint: "<advisory-url-or-draft>"
---
Prepare a security advisory for {{ arguments }}.

Inspect the advisory metadata, affected code, history, releases, version
ranges, references, and existing fix independently. Record any source material
that could not be accessed. Determine the affected and patched versions, then
propose severity and a CVSS vector with the disputed metrics explained.

Draft a concise advisory with summary, technical details, impact, affected
versions, solution, recommendations, timeline, credits when applicable, and
references. Do not include a copy-pastable exploit. Do not publish, change
advisory state, update a remote system, or request a CVE without explicit user
approval.
